[{"id":81138,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Duality.20is.20Duality/near/81138\">#1</a> It finally dawned on us that the analysis <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables#v2pdf\">here</a> from <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Hypothesis%20H\">Hypothesis H</a> exhibits holographic gauge/gravity duality as concrete mathematical duality. Now on <a href=\"https://twitter.com/SchreiberUrs/status/1217163007849050113\">p. 4 of v2</a>.</p>\n<p>Comments are welcome.</p>","timestamp":1579029349,"subject":"Duality is Duality","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":81153,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Duality.20is.20Duality/near/81153\">#2</a> This is a case of <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Koszul%20duality\">Koszul duality</a>? I see at this <a href=\"https://mathoverflow.net/questions/329/what-is-koszul-duality/394#394\">MO answer</a>, an instance is given as </p>\n<blockquote>\n<ol>\n<li>the relation between the homotopy groups of a topological space and its (co)homology groups</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n<p>In your case, how does the duality between homology and cohomology produce that shift of dimension from bulk to boundary, if that makes sense?</p>","timestamp":1579077372,"subject":"Duality is Duality","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":81155,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Duality.20is.20Duality/near/81155\">#3</a> Is term ‘co-observable’ as used in physics new with you? It seems computer scientists use it in a coalgebraic setting for the supervisory control of discrete-event systems.</p>","timestamp":1579078112,"subject":"Duality is Duality","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":81157,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Duality.20is.20Duality/near/81157\">#4</a> Yeah, my first thought was whether this relates to <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/holography%20as%20Koszul%20duality\">holography as Koszul duality</a>. But at this point, all we see is plain linear duality of Hopf algebras.</p>\n<p>In this context, the bulk/boundary correspondence is very much brought about by the simple fact that round chord diagrams and <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Jacobi%20diagrams\">Jacobi diagrams</a> have a bulk and a boundary.</p>","timestamp":1579078494,"subject":"Duality is Duality","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":81158,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Duality.20is.20Duality/near/81158\">#5</a> Yes, “co-observable” is something I just made up, in need of a term. But they do form a co-algebra, as any homology does!</p>\n<p>A more fancy terminology for the spectrum of co-observables is: The <em>motive</em> of the phase space:</p>\n<p>Let <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{Phase}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Phase</span></span></span></span></span> be a phase space, and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span></span></span></span> a ring spectrum, in the given ambient cohesive <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span></span></span></span>-topos. Then <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span></span></span></span>-valued observables are  <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[\\Sigma^\\infty {\\mathrm{Phase}}, E]</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">Σ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∞</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Phase</span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span>, while <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span></span></span></span>-value co-observables are <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∧</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E \\wedge \\Sigma^\\infty {\\mathrm{Phase}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∧</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">Σ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∞</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Phase</span></span></span></span></span></span>. But the geometric suspension spectrum <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Sigma^\\infty {\\mathrm{Phase}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">Σ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∞</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Phase</span></span></span></span></span></span>, that’s the motive of phase space.</p>","timestamp":1579078932,"subject":"Duality is Duality","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]}]